              "text": "(iii) Each of the Servicer and the Marketing Agent, severally and not jointly, will indemnify the Issuer against any third-party claim that the systems, software, reports or other deliverables it provides in performing its obligations under the Transaction Documents infringe any intellectual property right, except to the extent the claim arises from modifications made by the Issuer, the Issuer's combination of those items with items not supplied by the Servicer or the Marketing Agent, or the Issuer's specifications. In that event the Servicer or the Marketing Agent, as applicable, will procure the right to continue using the affected item, or modify or replace it so that it is non-infringing, and if none of the foregoing is available on commercially reasonable terms, refund the fees paid for the affected item. The aggregate liability of the Servicer and the Marketing Agent under this clause (iii) will not exceed 3x the annual fees payable to it under the Transaction Documents.",
